   The Fighter Drone is a high-performance autonomous defense platform defined by its advanced monocoque construction. Its hull is a single, seamless unit printed at the molecular level, featuring a dense, oblong central core that transitions into four elegant, organically curved spars. These supports branch outward to house "sounded" engine pods, creating a high-torque "X" configuration that allows for near-instantaneous Newtonian maneuvers. Because the frame is 3D-fabricated with precision-engineered voids, all critical "guts"—including the AI core, reactor, and weapon systems—are slotted into the chassis as modular inserts, allowing for rapid field repairs or total hull recycling.
   The craft’s lethality stems from a mathematically perfect 12-point turret grid that ensures true omnidirectional fire. Four 0.75m ball-turret Projected Particle Cannons (PPCs) are recessed into the interstitial gaps between the engine spars, providing heavy-impact "shield breaking" capabilities against larger targets. This primary array is supplemented by eight 0.5m ball-turret high-frequency lasers staggered at 45-degree offsets toward the front and rear faces of the hull. This dense interlocking field of fire, managed by a decentralized AI, allows the drone to act as a mobile spherical fortress, simultaneously neutralizing swarms of incoming missiles while systematically dismantling the subsystems of larger enemy warships.


